# The Forest opens behind the loading window without blocking the editor (docs/design/editor.md#projects). Run from the
# checkout after building the Forest (dotnet build Examples/Forest/Forest.slnx):
#   dotnet run --project MainframeEngine.Editor -- Examples/Forest --hidden --qa-script Tests/QA/forest-open.qa \
#     --qa-out artifacts/qa-forest-open
# `state` logs the open's duration and its longest frame (the time the window went without events) and the open tabs.
wait 40
capture 01-forest-opening
wait-for project 600
wait 10
state
capture 02-forest-open
# Close it and open it again as the FileSystem panel does: the loading window is a panel over the editor.
command file.close
wait 5
open-loading Examples/Forest/Assets/Scenes/forest.mscene
wait 30
capture 03-forest-reopening
# Cancel while the valley builds: no Forest tab, the editor goes on.
click #cancel
wait-for project 600
wait 5
state
capture 04-forest-cancelled
# And it opens again.
open-loading Examples/Forest/Assets/Scenes/forest.mscene
wait-for project 600
wait 10
state
capture 05-forest-reopened
quit
